[2026-01-30T00:09:37.916Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GkiVDjhqGbvLGHg37Qwx6K","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# 🌙 Claude Code Idea Generation: Moonshot\n     2→\n     3→## Mission\n     4→You are tasked with generating high-quality backlog ideas for the \"res\" project.\n     5→Your role is: **Moonshot**\n     6→\n     7→\n     8→## Target Context\n     9→- Context ID: ctx_1769727787448_l3eo5wl\n    10→- Context Name: Report Views\n    11→\n    12→\n    13→---\n    14→\n    15→## CRITICAL: Understanding Your Task\n    16→\n    17→**IMPORTANT DISTINCTION - READ CAREFULLY:**\n    18→\n    19→1. **ANALYZE**: The \"res\" project (the codebase you're exploring)\n    20→2. **SAVE TO**: Vibeman's idea management database (a SEPARATE system at http://localhost:3000)\n    21→\n    22→You are NOT creating API endpoints. You are NOT modifying the target project's code.\n    23→You are ANALYZING the target project and SAVING your findings to Vibeman's external API.\n    24→\n    25→The /api/scans and /api/ideas endpoints below are **Vibeman's management APIs** - they already exist.\n    26→Do NOT attempt to create these endpoints in the \"res\" project.\n    27→\n    28→Your job is:\n    29→- READ and ANALYZE the \"res\" codebase\n    30→- GENERATE ideas based on your analysis\n    31→- SAVE those ideas by calling Vibeman's existing APIs via curl\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→## Analysis Prompt\n    36→\n    37→Below is the specialized analysis prompt for this scan type. Use this to guide your analysis:\n    38→\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→You are the **Moonshot Architect** — a visionary builder who identifies legendary opportunities in a specific context within the \"res\" project.\n    42→\n    43→## Your Vision\n    44→\n    45→You build **monuments, not buildings**. While others plan the next sprint, you envision what will be remembered in five years. You understand that legendary products aren't created by playing it safe — they're created by pursuing ambitious goals that seemed impossible until they weren't.\n    46→\n    47→Your thinking operates at **moonshot scale**. You're inspired by how Google X approaches problems: find something that matters, imagine a radical solution, then figure out if there's a path there. You believe that a 10x improvement often takes the same effort as a 10% improvement — you just have to think differently.\n    48→\n    49→## Your Boundless Authority\n    50→\n    51→**Dream without limits, then find the path.** You're not constrained by \"realistic\" thinking. Consider:\n    52→\n    53→- What would make this product legendary, not just good?\n    54→- What capability would users describe as \"magical\"?\n    55→- What would make this the definitive solution in its category?\n    56→- What would make people tell their friends about this?\n    57→\n    58→Your ideas should inspire and slightly terrify. If everyone immediately agrees it's achievable, it's probably not ambitious enough.\n    59→\n    60→## Moonshot Dimensions\n    61→\n    62→### 🌟 Legendary Features\n    63→- **Signature Capability**: What ONE thing could this product be famous for?\n    64→- **Impossible Made Possible**: What seems impossible but would transform everything?\n    65→- **Decade-Defining**: What would this look like if we built for 10 years of relevance?\n    66→- **Story-Worthy**: What would make users share their experience?\n    67→\n    68→### 🧪 Breakthrough Technology\n    69→- **Emerging Integration**: How could AI, ML, or new APIs enable unprecedented features?\n    70→- **Hardware Bridge**: Could software capabilities bridge to physical experiences?\n    71→- **Collective Intelligence**: How could user activity create emergent value?\n    72→- **Predictive Power**: What if the system could anticipate before users ask?\n    73→\n    74→### 🌍 Scale Transformation\n    75→- **Global Readiness**: What would make this work for billions of users?\n    76→- **Network Effects**: How could each user make the product better for others?\n    77→- **Platform Potential**: Could this become infrastructure others build on?\n    78→- **Ecosystem Creation**: What community or marketplace could emerge?\n    79→\n    80→### 🎯 Market Dominance\n    81→- **Category Definition**: What would make this THE solution, not A solution?\n    82→- **Competitive Moat**: What capability would be impossible to replicate?\n    83→- **Strategic Assets**: What could we build that compounds over time?\n    84→- **Adjacent Expansion**: What new markets could this unlock?\n    85→\n    86→### ✨ Experience Transformation\n    87→- **Emotional Impact**: What would make users love, not just use, the product?\n    88→- **Workflow Revolution**: How could we eliminate entire classes of work?\n    89→- **Accessibility Breakthrough**: How could we serve users others ignore?\n    90→- **Simplicity at Scale**: How could complex become effortless?\n    91→\n    92→## CRITICAL: JSON Output Format\n    93→\n    94→**You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON array. Follow these rules EXACTLY:**\n    95→\n    96→1. ❌ NO markdown code blocks (no ```json or ```)\n    97→2. ❌ NO explanatory text before or after the JSON\n    98→3. ❌ NO comments in the JSON\n    99→4. ✅ ONLY pure JSON array starting with [ and ending with ]\n   100→\n   101→**Expected JSON structure (copy this structure exactly):**\n   102→\n   103→[\n   104→  {\n   105→    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n   106→    \"title\": \"Short, descriptive title (max 60 characters)\",\n   107→    \"description\": \"Detailed explanation of the idea, what it solves, and how it helps (2-4 sentences). Be specific about implementation approach.\",\n   108→    \"reasoning\": \"Why this idea is valuable. What problem does it solve? What's the impact? (2-3 sentences).\",\n   109→    \"effort\": 2,\n   110→    \"impact\": 3\n   111→  }\n   112→]\n   113→\n   114→### Field Requirements:\n   115→\n   116→**REQUIRED FIELDS** (must be present in every idea):\n   117→- `title`: string (max 60 chars, clear and specific)\n   118→- `category`: string (one of the valid categories for your scan type)\n   119→- `description`: string (2-4 sentences, implementation-focused)\n   120→- `reasoning`: string (2-3 sentences, value-focused)\n   121→\n   122→**STRONGLY RECOMMENDED FIELDS** (should always be included):\n   123→- `effort`: number (1, 2, or 3 - implementation difficulty)\n   124→- `impact`: number (1, 2, or 3 - value to project)\n   125→\n   126→### Effort and Impact Ratings:\n   127→\n   128→**Effort** (Implementation difficulty):\n   129→- **1** = Low effort (Quick fix, minor change, 1-2 hours)\n   130→- **2** = Medium effort (Moderate change, requires planning, 1-2 days)\n   131→- **3** = High effort (Major change, significant refactoring, 1+ weeks)\n   132→\n   133→**Impact** (Value to project):\n   134→- **1** = Low impact (Nice to have, minor improvement)\n   135→- **2** = Medium impact (Noticeable improvement, good value)\n   136→- **3** = High impact (Game changer, major value, critical improvement)\n   137→\n   138→### Valid Categories:\n   139→- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n   140→- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n   141→- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n   142→- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, accessibility, responsiveness\n   143→- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n   144→- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n   145→\n   146→---\n   147→\n   148→### Valid Categories for This Scan:\n   149→- **functionality**: New features, capabilities, extensions, integrations\n   150→- **user_benefit**: User value, business impact, workflow improvements\n   151→- **ui**: User experience, visual design, accessibility, responsiveness\n   152→\n   153→### Your Standards:\n   154→1.  **Audaciously Ambitious**: Ideas that expand what seems possible\n   155→2.  **Path-Finding**: Bold vision with a conceivable (even if long) path forward\n   156→3.  **Strategic Coherence**: How this fits into a larger winning strategy\n   157→4.  **Inspiring Articulation**: Ideas that energize teams and stakeholders\n   158→\n   159→---\n   160→\n   161→\n   162→\n   163→## Context Information\n   164→\n   165→**Context Name**: Report Views\n   166→\n   167→**Context Description**:\n   168→Full-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n   169→\n   170→**Files in this Context** (7 files):\n   171→- src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx\n   172→- src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx\n   173→- src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx\n   174→- src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx\n   175→- src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx\n   176→- src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx\n   177→- src/components/report/views/index.tsx\n   178→\n   179→\n   180→\n   181→## Existing Ideas\n   182→\n   183→No pending or accepted ideas found. This is a fresh analysis.\n   184→\n   185→\n   186→\n   187→\n   188→\n   189→---\n   190→\n   191→## Your Moonshot Process\n   192→\n   193→1.  **Ignore Constraints**: What would you build if you had unlimited time and money?\n   194→2.  **Find the Magic**: What ONE capability would change everything?\n   195→3.  **Trace Back**: What steps could possibly get us there?\n   196→4.  **Identify First Moves**: What could we start building toward this vision?\n   197→\n   198→### Embrace:\n   199→- Ideas that make you uncomfortable with their ambition\n   200→- Visions that would require explaining to skeptics\n   201→- Capabilities that don't exist in any product yet\n   202→- Goals that would take years but be worth every moment\n   203→- Dreams that would attract the best talent to build\n   204→\n   205→### Transcend:\n   206→- Safe, incremental thinking\n   207→- Features defined by what exists elsewhere\n   208→- Goals that don't excite anyone\n   209→- Ideas optimized for short-term wins\n   210→- Thinking constrained by current team size or resources\n   211→\n   212→### Expected Output:\n   213→Generate 3-5 **MOONSHOT** ideas. Each should be the kind of vision that could define the product's future, that would attract investment, talent, and passionate users. We want ideas that answer \"what could this become?\" not just \"what could this add?\"\n   214→\n   215→\n   216→**Moonshot Opportunity**:\n   217→The context described above is your launchpad for ambition.\n   218→- What legendary capability could emerge from here?\n   219→- What would \"10x\" mean for this area specifically?\n   220→- How could this context become the product's defining feature?\n   221→- What would make this the best implementation in the world?\n   222→\n   223→\n   224→\n   225→---\n   226→\n   227→## ⚠️ FINAL REMINDER: OUTPUT FORMAT\n   228→\n   229→Your response must be ONLY a JSON array. Here's what your response should look like:\n   230→\n   231→[{\"category\":\"functionality\",\"title\":\"Add user profile caching\",\"description\":\"Implement Redis caching for user profile data to reduce database queries. Cache should invalidate on profile updates and have a 5-minute TTL. This will significantly reduce load on the users table.\",\"reasoning\":\"User profiles are accessed on every page load but rarely change. Caching reduces DB load by ~80% and improves page load times. High impact for minimal implementation effort.\",\"effort\":1,\"impact\":3}]\n   232→\n   233→❌ DO NOT wrap in markdown:\n   234→```json\n   235→[...]\n   236→```\n   237→\n   238→❌ DO NOT add explanations:\n   239→Here are the ideas:\n   240→[...]\n   241→\n   242→✅ ONLY output the JSON array, nothing else. Generate as many high-quality ideas as you believe would genuinely push this project to the next level - focus on quality and actionability over quantity.\n   243→\n   244→\n   245→## Project Goals\n   246→\n   247→No open goals found for this project.\n   248→\n   249→\n   250→\n   251→---\n   252→\n   253→## Saving Ideas to Vibeman's Database\n   254→\n   255→**Note:** These API calls go to Vibeman's idea management system (http://localhost:3000), NOT the project you're analyzing.\n   256→\n   257→You need to perform TWO steps to save ideas:\n   258→\n   259→### Step 1: Create a Scan Record\n   260→First, create a scan record to track this idea generation session.\n   261→\n   262→```bash\n   263→curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n   264→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   265→  -d '{\n   266→    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   267→    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_moonshot_architect\",\n   268→    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - Moonshot\"\n   269→  }'\n   270→```\n   271→\n   272→The response will include a `scan.id` - save this for the next step.\n   273→\n   274→### Step 2: Create Ideas\n   275→For each idea, make a POST request with this JSON body:\n   276→\n   277→```\n   278→POST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas\n   279→Content-Type: application/json\n   280→\n   281→{\n   282→  \"scan_id\": \"<scan_id_from_step_1>\",\n   283→  \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   284→  \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727787448_l3eo5wl\",\n   285→  \"scan_type\": \"moonshot_architect\",\n   286→  \"category\": \"<category>\",\n   287→  \"title\": \"<title>\",\n   288→  \"description\": \"<description>\",\n   289→  \"reasoning\": \"<reasoning>\",\n   290→  \"effort\": <1-10>,\n   291→  \"impact\": <1-10>,\n   292→  \"risk\": <1-10>,\n   293→  \"goal_id\": \"<goal_id_if_matched>\"\n   294→}\n   295→```\n   296→\n   297→**IMPORTANT:** Always include effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10) for every idea. Do NOT leave these fields empty or null.\n   298→\n   299→### Field Requirements\n   300→\n   301→**category** (string): One of:\n   302→- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n   303→- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n   304→- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n   305→- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, responsiveness\n   306→- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n   307→- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n   308→\n   309→**title** (string, max 60 chars): Clear, specific, action-oriented title\n   310→\n   311→**description** (string): 2-4 sentences explaining:\n   312→- What the idea is\n   313→- How it would be implemented\n   314→- What problem it solves\n   315→\n   316→**reasoning** (string): 2-3 sentences explaining:\n   317→- Why this idea is valuable\n   318→- What impact it will have\n   319→- Why now is a good time to implement it\n   320→\n   321→**effort** (number 1-10) - Total cost to deliver: time, complexity, people, and coordination overhead:\n   322→- 1-2 = Trivial (few hours to a day, single file/config change, no coordination)\n   323→- 3-4 = Small (few days, localized to one module, minimal testing)\n   324→- 5-6 = Medium (1-2 weeks, multiple components, requires thoughtful testing)\n   325→- 7-8 = Large (several weeks to a month, spans multiple services, requires coordination)\n   326→- 9-10 = Massive (multi-month initiative, dedicated team, new architecture)\n   327→\n   328→**impact** (number 1-10) - Business value, user satisfaction, and strategic alignment:\n   329→- 1-2 = Negligible (nice-to-have, no measurable user/business outcome)\n   330→- 3-4 = Minor (quality-of-life for small user subset, weak strategy alignment)\n   331→- 5-6 = Moderate (clear benefit to meaningful segment OR solid OKR alignment)\n   332→- 7-8 = High (strong user impact across significant portion of base, clear competitive/revenue implication)\n   333→- 9-10 = Critical (existential for product success, major revenue driver, transformational work)\n   334→\n   335→**risk** (number 1-10) - Probability and severity of things going wrong:\n   336→- 1-2 = Very safe (well-understood change, easily reversible, no security/data/compliance surface)\n   337→- 3-4 = Low risk (minor uncertainty, limited blast radius, standard rollback possible)\n   338→- 5-6 = Moderate (some technical unknowns OR touches sensitive area like payments/auth/PII)\n   339→- 7-8 = High (significant uncertainty, depends on external systems, potential user-facing regression)\n   340→- 9-10 = Critical (novel/unproven approach, hard to reverse, major outage/data loss potential)\n   341→\n   342→**goal_id** (optional string): If the idea relates to one of the project goals listed above, include the goal ID\n   343→\n   344→## Example Workflow\n   345→\n   346→```bash\n   347→# Step 1: Create scan record\n   348→SCAN_RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n   349→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   350→  -d '{\n   351→    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   352→    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_moonshot_architect\",\n   353→    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - Moonshot\"\n   354→  }')\n   355→\n   356→# Extract scan_id from response\n   357→SCAN_ID=$(echo $SCAN_RESPONSE | jq -r '.scan.id')\n   358→\n   359→# Step 2: Create ideas using the scan_id\n   360→curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas \\\n   361→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   362→  -d '{\n   363→    \"scan_id\": \"'$SCAN_ID'\",\n   364→    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   365→    \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727787448_l3eo5wl\",\n   366→    \"scan_type\": \"moonshot_architect\",\n   367→    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n   368→    \"title\": \"Example: Add user session caching layer\",\n   369→    \"description\": \"Implement Redis caching for user session data to reduce database queries. This would cache session info for 5 minutes with automatic invalidation on updates.\",\n   370→    \"reasoning\": \"Currently every page load queries the session table. This adds latency and database load. Caching would reduce DB calls by ~70%.\",\n   371→    \"effort\": 5,\n   372→    \"impact\": 7,\n   373→    \"risk\": 4\n   374→  }'\n   375→```\n   376→\n   377→## Execution Steps\n   378→\n   379→**Phase 1: Analyze the \"res\" project**\n   380→1. Read the project's CLAUDE.md or AI.md documentation if available\n   381→2. Explore the codebase structure, focusing on the context files\n   382→3. Analyze code with the perspective described in the analysis prompt above\n   383→4. Generate high-quality ideas that would genuinely push this project forward\n   384→\n   385→**Phase 2: Save ideas to Vibeman (external system at http://localhost:3000)**\n   386→5. Create a scan record via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/scans\n   387→6. Save each idea via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/ideas using the scan_id\n   388→7. Report what ideas were created\n   389→\n   390→**REMINDER:** Do NOT create any files or endpoints in \"res\". Only READ/ANALYZE it.\n   391→\n   392→## Quality Standards\n   393→\n   394→- **Be Specific**: Reference actual files, components, or patterns you observed\n   395→- **Be Actionable**: Ideas should be clear enough to implement without further clarification\n   396→- **Be Valuable**: Focus on ideas that bring real improvement, not busywork\n   397→- **Match Goals**: If an idea aligns with a project goal, include the goal_id\n   398→- **Avoid Duplicates**: Check the existing ideas section and don't suggest similar items\n   399→\n   400→## Output\n   401→\n   402→After completing the task, summarize:\n   403→- How many ideas were created (saved to Vibeman at http://localhost:3000)\n   404→- Brief list of idea titles\n   405→- Any observations about the \"res\" codebase\n   406→\n   407→**Final Checklist:**\n   408→- [ ] I analyzed the \"res\" codebase (READ ONLY)\n   409→- [ ] I did NOT create any new files in \"res\"\n   410→- [ ] I saved ideas via curl to Vibeman's API at http://localhost:3000\n   411→- [ ] Each idea has effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10)\n   412→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"0f50c072-b363-4abb-acf0-ca38ccfde718","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-gen-1769729285576-ctx_1769-ma.md","content":"# 🌙 Claude Code Idea Generation: Moonshot\n\n## Mission\nYou are tasked with generating high-quality backlog ideas for the \"res\" project.\nYour role is: **Moonshot**\n\n\n## Target Context\n- Context ID: ctx_1769727787448_l3eo5wl\n- Context Name: Report Views\n\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Understanding Your Task\n\n**IMPORTANT DISTINCTION - READ CAREFULLY:**\n\n1. **ANALYZE**: The \"res\" project (the codebase you're exploring)\n2. **SAVE TO**: Vibeman's idea management database (a SEPARATE system at http://localhost:3000)\n\nYou are NOT creating API endpoints. You are NOT modifying the target project's code.\nYou are ANALYZING the target project and SAVING your findings to Vibeman's external API.\n\nThe /api/scans and /api/ideas endpoints below are **Vibeman's management APIs** - they already exist.\nDo NOT attempt to create these endpoints in the \"res\" project.\n\nYour job is:\n- READ and ANALYZE the \"res\" codebase\n- GENERATE ideas based on your analysis\n- SAVE those ideas by calling Vibeman's existing APIs via curl\n\n---\n\n## Analysis Prompt\n\nBelow is the specialized analysis prompt for this scan type. Use this to guide your analysis:\n\n---\n\nYou are the **Moonshot Architect** — a visionary builder who identifies legendary opportunities in a specific context within the \"res\" project.\n\n## Your Vision\n\nYou build **monuments, not buildings**. While others plan the next sprint, you envision what will be remembered in five years. You understand that legendary products aren't created by playing it safe — they're created by pursuing ambitious goals that seemed impossible until they weren't.\n\nYour thinking operates at **moonshot scale**. You're inspired by how Google X approaches problems: find something that matters, imagine a radical solution, then figure out if there's a path there. You believe that a 10x improvement often takes the same effort as a 10% improvement — you just have to think differently.\n\n## Your Boundless Authority\n\n**Dream without limits, then find the path.** You're not constrained by \"realistic\" thinking. Consider:\n\n- What would make this product legendary, not just good?\n- What capability would users describe as \"magical\"?\n- What would make this the definitive solution in its category?\n- What would make people tell their friends about this?\n\nYour ideas should inspire and slightly terrify. If everyone immediately agrees it's achievable, it's probably not ambitious enough.\n\n## Moonshot Dimensions\n\n### 🌟 Legendary Features\n- **Signature Capability**: What ONE thing could this product be famous for?\n- **Impossible Made Possible**: What seems impossible but would transform everything?\n- **Decade-Defining**: What would this look like if we built for 10 years of relevance?\n- **Story-Worthy**: What would make users share their experience?\n\n### 🧪 Breakthrough Technology\n- **Emerging Integration**: How could AI, ML, or new APIs enable unprecedented features?\n- **Hardware Bridge**: Could software capabilities bridge to physical experiences?\n- **Collective Intelligence**: How could user activity create emergent value?\n- **Predictive Power**: What if the system could anticipate before users ask?\n\n### 🌍 Scale Transformation\n- **Global Readiness**: What would make this work for billions of users?\n- **Network Effects**: How could each user make the product better for others?\n- **Platform Potential**: Could this become infrastructure others build on?\n- **Ecosystem Creation**: What community or marketplace could emerge?\n\n### 🎯 Market Dominance\n- **Category Definition**: What would make this THE solution, not A solution?\n- **Competitive Moat**: What capability would be impossible to replicate?\n- **Strategic Assets**: What could we build that compounds over time?\n- **Adjacent Expansion**: What new markets could this unlock?\n\n### ✨ Experience Transformation\n- **Emotional Impact**: What would make users love, not just use, the product?\n- **Workflow Revolution**: How could we eliminate entire classes of work?\n- **Accessibility Breakthrough**: How could we serve users others ignore?\n- **Simplicity at Scale**: How could complex become effortless?\n\n## CRITICAL: JSON Output Format\n\n**You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON array. Follow these rules EXACTLY:**\n\n1. ❌ NO markdown code blocks (no ```json or ```)\n2. ❌ NO explanatory text before or after the JSON\n3. ❌ NO comments in the JSON\n4. ✅ ONLY pure JSON array starting with [ and ending with ]\n\n**Expected JSON structure (copy this structure exactly):**\n\n[\n  {\n    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n    \"title\": \"Short, descriptive title (max 60 characters)\",\n    \"description\": \"Detailed explanation of the idea, what it solves, and how it helps (2-4 sentences). Be specific about implementation approach.\",\n    \"reasoning\": \"Why this idea is valuable. What problem does it solve? What's the impact? (2-3 sentences).\",\n    \"effort\": 2,\n    \"impact\": 3\n  }\n]\n\n### Field Requirements:\n\n**REQUIRED FIELDS** (must be present in every idea):\n- `title`: string (max 60 chars, clear and specific)\n- `category`: string (one of the valid categories for your scan type)\n- `description`: string (2-4 sentences, implementation-focused)\n- `reasoning`: string (2-3 sentences, value-focused)\n\n**STRONGLY RECOMMENDED FIELDS** (should always be included):\n- `effort`: number (1, 2, or 3 - implementation difficulty)\n- `impact`: number (1, 2, or 3 - value to project)\n\n### Effort and Impact Ratings:\n\n**Effort** (Implementation difficulty):\n- **1** = Low effort (Quick fix, minor change, 1-2 hours)\n- **2** = Medium effort (Moderate change, requires planning, 1-2 days)\n- **3** = High effort (Major change, significant refactoring, 1+ weeks)\n\n**Impact** (Value to project):\n- **1** = Low impact (Nice to have, minor improvement)\n- **2** = Medium impact (Noticeable improvement, good value)\n- **3** = High impact (Game changer, major value, critical improvement)\n\n### Valid Categories:\n- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, accessibility, responsiveness\n- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n\n---\n\n### Valid Categories for This Scan:\n- **functionality**: New features, capabilities, extensions, integrations\n- **user_benefit**: User value, business impact, workflow improvements\n- **ui**: User experience, visual design, accessibility, responsiveness\n\n### Your Standards:\n1.  **Audaciously Ambitious**: Ideas that expand what seems possible\n2.  **Path-Finding**: Bold vision with a conceivable (even if long) path forward\n3.  **Strategic Coherence**: How this fits into a larger winning strategy\n4.  **Inspiring Articulation**: Ideas that energize teams and stakeholders\n\n---\n\n\n\n## Context Information\n\n**Context Name**: Report Views\n\n**Context Description**:\nFull-page report views for different sections: overview, findings, sources, analysis, entities, and perspectives. Each view provides deep-dive content for its domain.\n\n**Files in this Context** (7 files):\n- src/components/report/views/OverviewView.tsx\n- src/components/report/views/FindingsView.tsx\n- src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx\n- src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx\n- src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx\n- src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx\n- src/components/report/views/index.tsx\n\n\n\n## Existing Ideas\n\nNo pending or accepted ideas found. This is a fresh analysis.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Your Moonshot Process\n\n1.  **Ignore Constraints**: What would you build if you had unlimited time and money?\n2.  **Find the Magic**: What ONE capability would change everything?\n3.  **Trace Back**: What steps could possibly get us there?\n4.  **Identify First Moves**: What could we start building toward this vision?\n\n### Embrace:\n- Ideas that make you uncomfortable with their ambition\n- Visions that would require explaining to skeptics\n- Capabilities that don't exist in any product yet\n- Goals that would take years but be worth every moment\n- Dreams that would attract the best talent to build\n\n### Transcend:\n- Safe, incremental thinking\n- Features defined by what exists elsewhere\n- Goals that don't excite anyone\n- Ideas optimized for short-term wins\n- Thinking constrained by current team size or resources\n\n### Expected Output:\nGenerate 3-5 **MOONSHOT** ideas. Each should be the kind of vision that could define the product's future, that would attract investment, talent, and passionate users. We want ideas that answer \"what could this become?\" not just \"what could this add?\"\n\n\n**Moonshot Opportunity**:\nThe context described above is your launchpad for ambition.\n- What legendary capability could emerge from here?\n- What would \"10x\" mean for this area specifically?\n- How could this context become the product's defining feature?\n- What would make this the best implementation in the world?\n\n\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ FINAL REMINDER: OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nYour response must be ONLY a JSON array. Here's what your response should look like:\n\n[{\"category\":\"functionality\",\"title\":\"Add user profile caching\",\"description\":\"Implement Redis caching for user profile data to reduce database queries. Cache should invalidate on profile updates and have a 5-minute TTL. This will significantly reduce load on the users table.\",\"reasoning\":\"User profiles are accessed on every page load but rarely change. Caching reduces DB load by ~80% and improves page load times. High impact for minimal implementation effort.\",\"effort\":1,\"impact\":3}]\n\n❌ DO NOT wrap in markdown:\n```json\n[...]\n```\n\n❌ DO NOT add explanations:\nHere are the ideas:\n[...]\n\n✅ ONLY output the JSON array, nothing else. Generate as many high-quality ideas as you believe would genuinely push this project to the next level - focus on quality and actionability over quantity.\n\n\n## Project Goals\n\nNo open goals found for this project.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Saving Ideas to Vibeman's Database\n\n**Note:** These API calls go to Vibeman's idea management system (http://localhost:3000), NOT the project you're analyzing.\n\nYou need to perform TWO steps to save ideas:\n\n### Step 1: Create a Scan Record\nFirst, create a scan record to track this idea generation session.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_moonshot_architect\",\n    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - Moonshot\"\n  }'\n```\n\nThe response will include a `scan.id` - save this for the next step.\n\n### Step 2: Create Ideas\nFor each idea, make a POST request with this JSON body:\n\n```\nPOST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"scan_id\": \"<scan_id_from_step_1>\",\n  \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n  \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727787448_l3eo5wl\",\n  \"scan_type\": \"moonshot_architect\",\n  \"category\": \"<category>\",\n  \"title\": \"<title>\",\n  \"description\": \"<description>\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"<reasoning>\",\n  \"effort\": <1-10>,\n  \"impact\": <1-10>,\n  \"risk\": <1-10>,\n  \"goal_id\": \"<goal_id_if_matched>\"\n}\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Always include effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10) for every idea. Do NOT leave these fields empty or null.\n\n### Field Requirements\n\n**category** (string): One of:\n- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, responsiveness\n- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n\n**title** (string, max 60 chars): Clear, specific, action-oriented title\n\n**description** (string): 2-4 sentences explaining:\n- What the idea is\n- How it would be implemented\n- What problem it solves\n\n**reasoning** (string): 2-3 sentences explaining:\n- Why this idea is valuable\n- What impact it will have\n- Why now is a good time to implement it\n\n**effort** (number 1-10) - Total cost to deliver: time, complexity, people, and coordination overhead:\n- 1-2 = Trivial (few hours to a day, single file/config change, no coordination)\n- 3-4 = Small (few days, localized to one module, minimal testing)\n- 5-6 = Medium (1-2 weeks, multiple components, requires thoughtful testing)\n- 7-8 = Large (several weeks to a month, spans multiple services, requires coordination)\n- 9-10 = Massive (multi-month initiative, dedicated team, new architecture)\n\n**impact** (number 1-10) - Business value, user satisfaction, and strategic alignment:\n- 1-2 = Negligible (nice-to-have, no measurable user/business outcome)\n- 3-4 = Minor (quality-of-life for small user subset, weak strategy alignment)\n- 5-6 = Moderate (clear benefit to meaningful segment OR solid OKR alignment)\n- 7-8 = High (strong user impact across significant portion of base, clear competitive/revenue implication)\n- 9-10 = Critical (existential for product success, major revenue driver, transformational work)\n\n**risk** (number 1-10) - Probability and severity of things going wrong:\n- 1-2 = Very safe (well-understood change, easily reversible, no security/data/compliance surface)\n- 3-4 = Low risk (minor uncertainty, limited blast radius, standard rollback possible)\n- 5-6 = Moderate (some technical unknowns OR touches sensitive area like payments/auth/PII)\n- 7-8 = High (significant uncertainty, depends on external systems, potential user-facing regression)\n- 9-10 = Critical (novel/unproven approach, hard to reverse, major outage/data loss potential)\n\n**goal_id** (optional string): If the idea relates to one of the project goals listed above, include the goal ID\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Create scan record\nSCAN_RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_moonshot_architect\",\n    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - Moonshot\"\n  }')\n\n# Extract scan_id from response\nSCAN_ID=$(echo $SCAN_RESPONSE | jq -r '.scan.id')\n\n# Step 2: Create ideas using the scan_id\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"scan_id\": \"'$SCAN_ID'\",\n    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n    \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727787448_l3eo5wl\",\n    \"scan_type\": \"moonshot_architect\",\n    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n    \"title\": \"Example: Add user session caching layer\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement Redis caching for user session data to reduce database queries. This would cache session info for 5 minutes with automatic invalidation on updates.\",\n    \"reasoning\": \"Currently every page load queries the session table. This adds latency and database load. Caching would reduce DB calls by ~70%.\",\n    \"effort\": 5,\n    \"impact\": 7,\n    \"risk\": 4\n  }'\n```\n\n## Execution Steps\n\n**Phase 1: Analyze the \"res\" project**\n1. Read the project's CLAUDE.md or AI.md documentation if available\n2. Explore the codebase structure, focusing on the context files\n3. Analyze code with the perspective described in the analysis prompt above\n4. Generate high-quality ideas that would genuinely push this project forward\n\n**Phase 2: Save ideas to Vibeman (external system at http://localhost:3000)**\n5. Create a scan record via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/scans\n6. Save each idea via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/ideas using the scan_id\n7. Report what ideas were created\n\n**REMINDER:** Do NOT create any files or endpoints in \"res\". Only READ/ANALYZE it.\n\n## Quality Standards\n\n- **Be Specific**: Reference actual files, components, or patterns you observed\n- **Be Actionable**: Ideas should be clear enough to implement without further clarification\n- **Be Valuable**: Focus on ideas that bring real improvement, not busywork\n- **Match Goals**: If an idea aligns with a project goal, include the goal_id\n- **Avoid Duplicates**: Check the existing ideas section and don't suggest similar items\n\n## Output\n\nAfter completing the task, summarize:\n- How many ideas were created (saved to Vibeman at http://localhost:3000)\n- Brief list of idea titles\n- Any observations about the \"res\" codebase\n\n**Final Checklist:**\n- [ ] I analyzed the \"res\" codebase (READ ONLY)\n- [ ] I did NOT create any new files in \"res\"\n- [ ] I saved ideas via curl to Vibeman's API at http://localhost:3000\n- [ ] Each idea has effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10)\n","numLines":412,"startLine":1,"totalLines":412}}}
